#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0410 expect=violation domain=SV
#note "Authority: SDTM/SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0410, Condition 'Scheduled or Contingent visit (exists in TV)', Rule 'VISITNUM identifies unique record within subject'. Subject S1-001 has TWO records with VISITNUM=2, a planned visit (TV defines 2), so VISITNUM does not identify a unique record within that subject -> rows 2 and 3 BOTH fire (neither record is uniquely identified; is_unique_set is false for every member of a repeated tuple). S1-002's single VISITNUM=2 (row 5) is unique within its own subject -> silent. Not a foreign-discrimination pin: the rule tests 'in', so a primary-bound read would also fire here; the discriminator is -valid_unplanned_duplicate-SV."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=S1-001 VISITNUM=2
#expectViolationAt row=3 USUBJID=S1-001 VISITNUM=2
dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVSTDTC  type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Visit"
---
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 1 | SCREENING | 2024-01-02
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 2 | BASELINE  | 2024-01-10
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 2 | BASELINE  | 2024-01-12
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 3 | WEEK 4    | 2024-02-07
S1 | SV | S1-002 | 2 | BASELINE  | 2024-01-11
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col TVSTRL   type=Char label="Visit Start Rule"
---
S1 | TV | 1 | SCREENING | Start of screening
S1 | TV | 2 | BASELINE  | Day 1
S1 | TV | 3 | WEEK 4    | Day 29
---
